<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Montaperti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1260">1260</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Montaperti was fought on 4 September 1260 near Siena between the Guelph army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> and a Ghibelline force of Siena, Florentine exiles under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farinata-degli-uberti">Farinata degli Uberti</a> and German cavalry sent by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manfred-king-of-sicily">Manfred of Sicily</a>. The Florentines were routed with heavy losses, and the Ghibellines took over Florence, which they held until after the Angevin victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a> in 1266.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-montaperti.jpg" alt="Battle of Montaperti" width="320" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:How_the_Florentines_raised_an_army_to_fortify_Montalcino_and_were_discomfited_by_Count_Giordano_and_by_the_Sienese_at_Montaperti.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
